---
title: Rosemary Thyme Brown Butter Rice Krispies Treats with Pecans
servings: 2
prep-time: 15 minutes
cook-time: 20 minutes
tags: [thanksgiving, Desserts, brown-butter, Holiday recipes, Rice Krispies treats]
source: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DQzNuW-EdcR/
image: https://scontent-iad3-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.71878-15/574629332_810767681708934_7398954640191379444_n.jpg?stp=cmp1_dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=111&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0xJUFMuYmVzdF9pbWFnZV91cmxnZW4uQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=MoZyfZiS-GoQ7kNvwGL_eWT&_nc_oc=Adn-XQU3gE44vu4gQUKcjV_pv1qFyDy39XG5Y-WUkLj9R_sxaEIA-yO0pHv9LohSClM&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=VBSkvqzglyLJNL-67eXJ4A&oh=00_Afk4tXOuVntHPVLu69P1svYY10m8iZpfNrFsR744UjZJBQ&oe=694C9151
---

In a skillet, brown @butter{2%tablespoons} over medium heat until golden and nutty; then add @rosemary{1%tsp} and @thyme{1%tsp} and stir to infuse their aroma. Remove from heat.

To the browned butter, add @marshmallows{3%cups} and stir until melted and smooth; then fold in @rice krispies cereal{4%cups} until evenly coated, and stir in @pecans{0.5%cups} for crunch.

Line a #baking dish{} with parchment paper and press the mixture into an even layer. Let cool for ~{15%minutes}, then cut into squares.